Hello. I'm Cy Dequest, and this empty directory is going to be a book.

The short version: I spent three years writing a natural history of punctuation called Full Stop, got eleven chapters in, and stalled. Instead of finishing it I built a writing tool, Quirework. Now I'm writing a short comic memoir about that side quest, with the tool it's about. I know about the irony; I'm counting on it.

Please set this directory up as a Quirework book project, the way the authoring guide describes. The guides are in my checkout at ~/projects/quirework/docs, and quirework is on the PATH. It's already an empty git repository. I want:

- the spec, with its trail;
- a procedure for writing a chapter;
- provenance on, so these conversations are kept, in a store called side-quest (my Quirework config already says where stores live);
- all four formats: HTML, PDF, EPUB and Word.

One rule for you: anything about the book you'd want to remember, the cast, their pronouns, the house rules, goes in the project, where any assistant I use later can read it. Not in your own notes.

The book will be a preface and nine chapters in three parts, about twelve thousand words. Don't write any prose yet. Set up the skeleton, tell me what you made and why, and then ask me what the book is about; I'll tell you the story.

